  (history ("claude" "2026-10-11" "Cloudstair (D50): the Windworn Arch answers H5. When you come to the arch carrying H5, its rose stone rings, and this plays once: a stone bell on H5's own F# (5 and 10 times D2), then a glass flute comes down through the mode the way the wind now goes, A G F# E D, past the Mixolydian C to A, and home on D with the stone ringing F# once more over it. Every F# is a drone-fm voice at cents -13.686, H5's just third, so it sits on the carried drone. About 11 s; a silent 5 s pattern lets it ring out. Channel 4 and 7 carry the bells so a held flute never cuts them."))))
